  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Guitar Solo** (1 review): A guitar solo appears between Lay Low and Gideon [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **MMJ2008-10-03.MG300** (recommended): source not stated; 23 songs; 141 min [1]\n- **MMJ2008-10-03.DPA4022**: source not stated; 21 songs; 141 min; rated 3/5 by 3 [2]. Said about its sound: The audio quality is described as good but somewhat muddy [3]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- The audience had a great vibe in the theater [3]\n- The attendee was riding the rail for this performance [5]\n- The user called it the most intense MMJ show of nine seen [5]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **MMJ2008-10-03.MG300**: taped by Lee Schultz; transferred by Soling; source: Microtech Gefell M300>V3>MT1@24/48 [1]. Also: DIN microphone clamped to lamp rail, first balcony, four feet down [1]\n- **MMJ2008-10-03.DPA4022**: taped by Soling; transferred by Soling; source: DPA 4022>V3>SD 702 @24/96 [2]. Also: ORTF pair clamped to first balcony rail, extended six feet out [2]\n\n## Art and photos\n\n- Poster by Jay Ryan: [My Morning Jacket Poster by Jay Ryan | Poster Cabaret](https://postercabaret.com/gallery/sold-out/my-morning-jacket-poster-by-jay-ryan/) [7]",
